{title: The old account was settled}
{subtitle: Hymnal 306}

{comment: Chorus}
Long ago, Long ago
Yes, the old account was settled long ago
And the record’s clear today, Jesus washed my sins away
When the old account was settled long ago

{comment: Verse 1}
There was a time on earth, When in the book of heaven
An old account was standing, For sins yet unforgiven
My name was at the top, And many things below
I went into the keeper, And settled long ago

{comment: Verse 2}
The old account was large, And growing every day
For I was always sinning, And never tried to pray
But when I looked ahead, And saw such pain and woe
I said that I would settle, I settled long ago

{comment: Verse 3}
When at the judgment bar, I stand before my King
And He the book will open, He cannot find a thing
Then will my heart be glad, While tears of joy will flow
Because I had it settled, And settled long ago

{comment: Verse 4}
When in that happy home, My Saviors home above
I’ll sing redemptions story, And praise Him for His love
I’ll not forget that book, With pages white as snow
Because I came and settled, And settled long ago

{comment: Verse 5}
O sinner, seek the Lord, Repent of all your sins
Thus He hath commanded, If you would enter in
And then if you should live A hundred years below
Up there you’ll not regret it, You settled it long ago
